---
system: sys-19-billing-subscription
flow_id: stripe-webhook-processing
surface: webhook-inbound
spec_anchor: /software/systems/19-billing-subscription#stripe-webhook
actors: [Stripe, Gateway, BillingService, SQS, NotificationService]
apis:
  - POST /webhooks/stripe
externals: [Stripe]
queues: [tjbot-billing-events]
failure_paths:
  - stripe_signature_invalid
  - duplicate_event_dedupe
  - webhook_persist_failed
  - worker_handler_failed
idempotency: Stripe-Signature header verified against tjbot/stripe/webhook-secret; webhook_events table PK on stripe_event_id deduplicates Stripe's at-least-once redelivery (Stripe retries up to 3x)
retry: synchronous handler MUST return 200 within 5s so Stripe stops retrying; downstream worker retries via SQS visibility-timeout + dead-letter queue
timeout: 5s p99 (Stripe SLA cutoff — exceeding triggers Stripe retry)
status: final
---
%% HAND-CURATED. Race-condition surfaced per plan §11: Stripe idempotency via {Stripe-Signature header verify + stripe_event_id PK insert} — duplicate webhook delivery cannot double-process.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Stripe
    participant Gateway
    participant BillingService
    participant SQS
    participant NotificationService

    Stripe->>Gateway: POST /webhooks/stripe + Stripe-Signature header + event payload
    Gateway->>BillingService: forward (no JWT — auth via Stripe-Signature only)
    BillingService->>BillingService: verify Stripe-Signature against webhook-secret (tjbot/stripe/webhook-secret)
    alt stripe_signature_invalid
        Note over BillingService: alert ops — potential webhook forgery
        BillingService-->>Gateway: 400 invalid_signature
        Gateway-->>Stripe: 400
    else signature valid
        BillingService->>BillingService: INSERT webhook_events {stripe_event_id, event_type, processing_status: "received"}
        alt duplicate_event_dedupe
            Note over BillingService: PK conflict on stripe_event_id — Stripe redelivery
            BillingService-->>Gateway: 200 OK (already processed)
            Gateway-->>Stripe: 200 OK
        else new event
            BillingService-)SQS: SendMessage tjbot-billing-events {stripe_event_id, event_type, payload_hash}
            alt webhook_persist_failed
                Note over BillingService: SQS send failed — webhook_events status: "failed" — Stripe will retry up to 3x
                BillingService-->>Gateway: 500 webhook_persist_failed
                Gateway-->>Stripe: 500
            else enqueued
                BillingService-->>Gateway: 200 OK (within 5s — Stripe done)
                Gateway-->>Stripe: 200 OK
            end
        end
    end

    Note over BillingService,NotificationService: async worker leg
    SQS-->>BillingService: dequeue webhook_event
    BillingService->>BillingService: handle by event_type (checkout.session.completed | customer.subscription.updated | invoice.payment_failed | ...) — rebuild entitlements, update subscription_status
    alt worker_handler_failed
        Note over BillingService: webhook_events status set to "failed", attempts++ — SQS visibility timeout returns it for retry, DLQ after N attempts
    else handler ok
        BillingService->>BillingService: webhook_events status: "processed", processed_at = now()
        BillingService-)NotificationService: enqueue user-facing notification (sys-10) — payment success / payment failed / trial ending
    end

    Note over Stripe,SQS: idempotency hinges on stripe_event_id PK — Stripe-Signature verify rejects forgery — 200-in-5s separates ingest from work
